  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Discover the beauty of Malawi - Dzawoneni Malawi okongola (DZAMA) - Department of Tourism (DoT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Direct Award Grant to the Department of Tourism. The &lt;strong&gt;overall objective (Impact)&lt;/strong&gt; is to contribute to Malawi&#xbf;s sustainable development of the ecotourism sector.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project intends to contribute to achieve specific objectives 1, 2 and 3, of the programme, in particular the following outputs: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 1.2: Capacity of local communities to manage and own ecotourism ventures enhanced, especially for women and youth business owners; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 1.3: Ecotourism attractions, products and services are certified and graded; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 2.1: Capacities for coordinating ecotourism developments improved at all levels; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 2.2: Research in the field of ecotourism strengthened; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 2.3: Information management systems for ecotourism enhanced; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 3.1: ICT based market oriented tools for awareness of Malawian tourism brand improved; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Output 3.2: Access to key source markets (both local and international) for ecotourism products enhanced.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specifically, the project will support the implementation of activities focusing on developing diverse and sustainable natural resource-based tourism products, strengthening institutional capacity at national, district, and local levels, and promoting Malawi as an ecotourism destination in domestic, regional, and international markets. The grant will facilitate the implementation of the 2020 Malawi Ecotourism Strategy, which aligns with the broader National Tourism Strategy and seeks to position Malawi as a leading tourist destination with well-preserved natural resources and a rich cultural heritage. Additionally, it will support the National Tourism Policy (2019) and the Malawi National Tourism Investment Masterplan (2022-2042), both of which provide a framework for structured tourism investment and the development of ecotourism and other tourism sectors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The action will be implemented across key tourism destinations in Malawi&apos;s Northern, Central, and Southern regions. In the Northern Region, interventions will focus on Misuku Hills, Manchewe Waterfalls, and Nkhata Bay. In the Central Region, the action will target the Chongoni Rock Art World Heritage Site, the Kasungu National Park buffer zone, and Nkhotakota Wildlife Reserve. In the Southern Region, activities will be implemented in the Elephant Marsh Community Conservation Area, the Mount Mulanje Biosphere Reserve, Zomba Plateau, and Lake Malawi National Park.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
